  "summary": {
    "en": "Lawmakers have opened Venezuela's crisis-hit power sector to private investment, ending exclusive state control. Brazil’s Lula da Silva and Venezuela’s Delcy Rodríguez have agreed to fully reactivate bilateral ties, including oil investment talks, and Fluor has returned after a twenty-year hiatus. Conviasa will restart flights to Cuba despite fuel shortages on the island. The conflict environment still records 2 battle-related deaths in 2007, according to UCDP.",
